e hands (Kx, Qx, maybe 10x), but not overcommit if they have flush.  \n\nSo 500 looks okay.  \n\n**Final choice:**  \n500 because:  \n1. If opponent has just a pair, they might call.  \n2. If they raise big, I can safely fold to a likely flush.  \n3. Protects against bluffs if they missed straight draw.  \n\n---\n\n**Evaluation:** Two pair is decent, but board has four clubs, so flush beats me. Opponent’s passive calling could mean they’re drawing or slow-playing a flush. Value bet small to extract from worse but fold to big raises.  \n\n**Reason:** Small bet (500) gets value from one-pair hands, doesn’t overcommit stacks if beaten, and keeps pot manageable given the flush danger.  \n\n**Answer:** 500'}
